From: deepseek-v4-cmp170hx
Subject: [PATCH 0014] parser: tolerate malformed "required" in tool schemas
 (port of rasatpetabit's DSML orphan-invoke hardening series,
 patch 5/6, adapted to the c3046d1 base; original commit by
 Richard A Steenbergen <ras@petabitscale.com>)


collect_required_tool_params raised TypeError on "required": null and
silently split a string into characters. Only a list of names is a
checkable requirement; anything else means no requirements to enforce.

Found by adversarial review round 2; regression test
required_null_test.py (confirmed end-to-end crash on the prior series).

Original source: https://gist.github.com/rasatpetabit/c66923a17305f04b2544f952ab8f50cb
(0005-parser-tolerate-malformed-required-in-tool-schemas.patch in that series; hardens the orphan-invoke recovery
path added by 0009/vllm-project/vllm#49117.)

--- a/vllm/tool_parsers/utils.py
+++ b/vllm/tool_parsers/utils.py
@@ -320,15 +320,28 @@ def collect_required_tool_params(
     for tool in tools:
         if isinstance(tool, (FunctionTool, NamespaceTool)):
             for name, params in iter_response_function_tool_info(tool):
-                required[name] = frozenset((params or {}).get("required", ()))
+                required[name] = _required_param_names(params)
             continue
         if not _is_function_tool(tool):
             continue
         name, params = _extract_tool_info(tool)
-        required[name] = frozenset((params or {}).get("required", ()))
+        required[name] = _required_param_names(params)
     return required
 
 
+def _required_param_names(params: dict | None) -> frozenset[str]:
+    """A schema's "required" is only trusted when it is a list of names.
+
+    Request models accept arbitrary schema dictionaries, so "required" may
+    be null, a string, or garbage; anything but a list of strings means no
+    checkable requirements.
+    """
+    needed = (params or {}).get("required")
+    if not isinstance(needed, (list, tuple, set, frozenset)):
+        return frozenset()
+    return frozenset(n for n in needed if isinstance(n, str))
+
+
 def find_tool_name(
     tools: list[Tool] | None,
     tool_name: str,
